<node id="11145633" title="Challenge: sort weekdays in week-order (elegantly and efficiently)" created="2022-07-21 10:08:27" updated="2022-07-21 10:08:27" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="1042">CUFP</type>
<author id="1165397">bliako</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;It just occured to me that I do not know how to sort weekdays in week-order except with this:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;c&gt;
my @weekdays = qw/Monday Saturday Thursday/;
my %order = (
        monday =&gt; 1,
        tuesday =&gt; 2,
        wednesday =&gt; 3,
        thursday =&gt; 4,
        friday =&gt; 5,
        saturday =&gt; 6,
        sunday =&gt; 7,
);
print join ",", map { $_-&gt;[0] } 
sort { $a-&gt;[1] &lt;=&gt; $b-&gt;[1] }
map { [$_, $order{lc $_}] } @weekdays;
&lt;/c&gt;

&lt;p&gt;is there a way without using that &lt;c&gt;%order&lt;/c&gt;?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;bw, bliako&lt;/p&gt;</doctext>
